WEBVTT

00:10:28.246 --> 00:10:30.329
I want to ask you about the
joy of being wrong.

00:10:30.704 --> 00:10:32.996
The place I wanted to begin
on this is to ask you,

00:10:33.371 --> 00:10:35.579
when you were growing up or
earlier in your life,

00:10:35.579 --> 00:10:37.329
how did you handle making mistakes?

00:10:40.537 --> 00:10:44.996
Hesitating because I can't it's not
that I didn't make any mistakes,

00:10:44.996 --> 00:10:48.996
I certainly made many, but I wasn't
very impressed by my mistakes.

00:10:48.996 --> 00:10:51.204
I mean, they were not very
salient in my life.

00:10:51.246 --> 00:10:53.704
So if you're asking about
my earlier, you know,

00:10:53.704 --> 00:10:58.246
as a student and so I don't have much
to report that I have an interest as

00:10:58.246 --> 00:11:04.162
a researcher, I found my mistakes
very instructive.